net: dsa: undo user VLAN setup when CPU-side registration fails

The user-port VLAN is programmed before dsa_port_host_vlan_add(). If host
registration fails, release the earlier user-port membership rather than
returning with hardware state for a VLAN device which was never created.
Keep the original host error and do not delete a host entry that failed
registration. Later address-filter allocation failures retain the existing
host-then-user unwind path.

--- a/net/dsa/user.c
+++ b/net/dsa/user.c
@@ -1825,7 +1825,7 @@
 		if (extack._msg)
 			netdev_err(dev, "CPU port %d: %s\n", dp->cpu_dp->index,
 				   extack._msg);
-		return ret;
+		goto rollback_user;
 	}
 
 	if (!dsa_switch_supports_uc_filtering(ds) &&
@@ -1865,6 +1865,7 @@
 
 rollback:
 	dsa_port_host_vlan_del(dp, &vlan);
+rollback_user:
 	dsa_port_vlan_del(dp, &vlan);
 
 	return ret;
